Based on the reproduction and stack trace, the problem is that ― as of #13085 ― vector-tile and other vector layers with a “background” are painted by simply setting the CSS backgroundColor on the layer’s DOM container.  That container is stacked above all lower‐level layers, so its background hides whatever is underneath.  Instead, we must keep the container transparent and draw the background into the canvas itself, before we render the tile/vector graphics.  

Below are two small *SEARCH/REPLACE* patches to `src/ol/renderer/canvas/VectorLayer.js` that

  1. Stop passing the background color into `useContainer()` (so the DOM element stays transparent), and  
  2. Immediately after we size/clear the canvas, draw a full‐canvas fillRect with the layer’s background color (if any).  

